          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Key Points"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.569,
            0.883,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The International System of Units (SI units) has been adopted by countries as standard units of measurement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.616,
            0.786,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The SI unit of length is metre. Its symbol is m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.899,
            0.115,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "96"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.642,
            0.77,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 km = 1000 m, 1 m = 100 cm, 1 cm = 10 mm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.668,
            0.882,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When distance is stated with respect to a fixed object or point, then this point is called a reference point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.715,
            0.882,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An object is said to be in motion if its position changes with respect to a reference point with time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.761,
            0.882,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When an object moves along a straight line, its motion is called linear motion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.808,
            0.882,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When an object moves along a circular path, its motion is called circular motion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.854,
            0.883,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When any object moves to and fro about any fixed position, its motion is called oscillatory motion."
            }
          ]
        },
